<p>If print results are not as required when using the RPCS printer driver, 
 try the procedures below.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you reinstall the printer driver or install 
 the latest printer driver, you may be get correct printing result that 
 you require, uninstall the old version before installing the new one.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Characters or images do not print out, or if they do, they 
 are printed incorrectly</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Spool Data in 
 EMF Format </span>check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span> in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Some extended characters are corrupted, or not print correctly</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span> in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span><span class="Term-Soft">
</span>list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Graphic data cannot be printed, or if possible, it is not printed 
 correctly</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Change the <span class="Term-Soft">Resolution:</span> setting on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Standard</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Settings</span> for <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Quality/Color</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> menu and change the setting for <span class="Term-Soft">Dithering:</span>, and then print.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Spool Data in 
 EMF Format </span>check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span> in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Patterns are not printed</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Shift Shading 
 Pattern</span> check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Enlarge Shading 
 Pattern</span> check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Change the <span class="Term-Soft">Resolution:</span> setting on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Standard</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Settings</span> for <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Quality/Color</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> menu and change the setting for <span class="Term-Soft">Dithering:</span>, and then print.</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Spool Data in 
 EMF Format </span>check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span> in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Even though the fill color of the pattern is the same, the 
 color changes according to the place or page</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Change the <span class="Term-Soft">Resolution:</span> setting on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Standard</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Settings</span> for <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Quality/Color</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> menu and change the setting for <span class="Term-Soft">Dithering:</span>, and then print.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Though <span class="Term-Soft">K (Black)</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Gray Reproduction:</span> list is selected, black and 
 gray areas of documents are printed in full color.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Vector</span> in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>If an image contains gray data, select the <span class="Term-Soft">K (Black) for Gray Pixels Only</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Gray 
 Reproduction:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Adjust Image Quality/Color</span> 
 tab.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Images cannot be printed, or if possible, they are not printed 
 correctly.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Spool Data in 
 EMF Format </span>check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span> in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Change Data Processing</span> 
 check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Change the <span class="Term-Soft">Resolution:</span> 
 setting on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Print quality is unsatisfactory</p>
<ul>
<li>Change the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Resolution: </span>setting on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Standard</span> menu.</li>
<li>If a document 
 contains images, change <span class="Term-Soft">Print Priority:</span> on 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> menu.</li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Print speed is slow</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Spool Data in 
 EMF Format </span>check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a lower resolution in the <span class="Term-Soft">Resolution:</span> 
 list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><p>If a document contains images, change <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Priority:</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
<li><p>If a document contains images, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Change Data Processing</span> check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>When printing in black and white, select <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span> 
 list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> menu. 
 Alternatively, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Change Data Processing</span> 
 check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Change <span class="Term-Soft">Job Load Distribution:</span> 
 on the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">It takes time for computer to be released from the printing 
 process</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Spool Data in 
 EMF Format </span>check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a lower resolution in the <span class="Term-Soft">Resolution:</span> 
 list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Shift Load to Printer</span> 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Load Distribution:</span> list on the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>If a document contains images, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Change Data Processing</span> check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><p>When printing in black and white, select <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span> 
 list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> menu. 
 Alternatively, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Change Data Processing</span> 
 check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Clicking Print button makes application close / Application 
 freezes</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Raster</span> in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Vector/Raster:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Change Data Processing</span> 
 check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Advanced</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Spool Data in 
 EMF Format </span>check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Printing PDF files results in a size error</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Near Standard 
 Size</span> check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Do not print or unexpectedly rotate the image by 90 degrees 
 and print it</p>
<ul>
<li><p>The paper size and type of input tray may not 
 match the physical settings.<br/>
 See <a href="~/Topics/IDH_DSETUPOPTION">Setting Up Options</a>, and configure 
 the correct settings in the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> tab.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" role="heading">Blank areas appear on multiple pages or page order is incorrect</p>
<p>If you are printing through the LPR port or Standard TCP/IP port, use 
 the following procedure to change the settings.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-OS">Devices and Printers</span> 
 window, open the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="2">
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-OS">Advanced</span> 
 tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">Start printing after 
 last page is spooled</span> and <span class="Term-OS">Print spooled documents 
 first</span>, and then click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Make test prints using various applications and 
 files.</p></li>
</ol>
